# Operational UI Architecture: **UMB-UI-004**

## The Diegetic Psychological Interface Constitution

**Target Architecture:** *Ashen Oath* — *Engine of Consequence*

---

# Constitutional Principle

> **The interface exists to communicate Kaelen's lived experience—not expose engine variables.**
>
> Every screen must answer a single psychological question while preserving complete mechanical truth.
>
> The player should never feel as though they are opening menus. They should feel as though they are opening another page of Kaelen's life.

---

# Design Pillars

Every interface element must satisfy four constitutional pillars.

## I. Mechanical Truth

The interface never lies about gameplay.

Hitboxes remain accurate.

Resources remain accurate.

Enemy positions remain accurate.

Cooldowns remain accurate.

The player may question Kaelen's interpretation of events—but never the underlying rules of combat.

Psychology influences perception.

It never falsifies reality.

---

## II. Psychological Translation

Engine variables are never presented directly.

Instead, every runtime value passes through three layers before reaching the player.

```
        ENGINE REALITY
      (Authoritative Runtime)

      FSoulStateVector
      Trust Bands
      Integration Debt
      Corruption
               │
               ▼
     Psychological Interpretation

    "Mind is Fracturing"

    "Garrett is Concerned"

    "Resolve is Steady"

               │
               ▼
      Somatic Presentation

 • handwriting changes

 • breathing

 • page movement

 • ink

 • posture

 • environmental audio
```

The player experiences the meaning of the variables rather than reading the variables themselves.

---

## III. World Authenticity

Every interface belongs somewhere inside the world.

Nothing exists simply because "games need menus."

| Interface     | World Object            |
| ------------- | ----------------------- |
| Inventory     | Kaelen's field pack     |
| Journal       | Personal field notebook |
| Lore          | Memory Palace           |
| Progression   | Heartstone Sanctuary    |
| Relationships | Campfire conversations  |
| Save Files    | Journey Journals        |

Whenever possible, the interface should feel physically present.

---

## IV. One Psychological Question Per Screen

Every screen has exactly one responsibility.

If a screen answers multiple unrelated questions, it should be divided.

| Screen               | Governing Question         |
| -------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Field Journal        | **What have we learned?**  |
| Equipment            | **What am I carrying?**    |
| Camp                 | **How are we doing?**      |
| Memory Constellation | **Why am I like this?**    |
| Heartstone Sanctuary | **Who do I become next?**  |
| Journey Archive      | **Which journey is this?** |

This prevents interface bloat while keeping navigation intuitive.

---

## V. Revelation (Uncertainty & Care)

Nothing appears before the player has a reason to care.

Interfaces, constellation nodes, and deep lore pages should reveal themselves organically in response to world encounters and emotional breakthroughs, rather than cluttering the screen from minute one.
---

# The Three Layers of Truth

The player should never see raw engine data unless they explicitly request advanced information.

## Layer I — Reality

Authoritative gameplay state.

```
IntegrationDebt = 0.81

Resolve = 0.67

Isolation = 0.42

GarrettTrust = 0.91
```

These values exist only for gameplay systems.

---

## Layer II — Interpretation

The engine translates numbers into psychological language.

```
Mind State

Fracturing

Resolve

Determined

Isolation

Withdrawing

Garrett

Watching You Carefully
```

This is the player's primary information layer.

---

## Layer III — Somatic Presentation

The interface expresses psychological state physically.

Examples include:

• handwriting becoming unstable

• pages turning more slowly

• breathing becoming shallow

• ink bleeding through paper

• bookmarks trembling

• subtle audio distortion

The interface itself becomes another storytelling system.

---

# Interface Architecture

## I. Field Journal

**Question**

"What have we learned?"

The journal is the root of the interface.

Rather than functioning as a codex, it becomes an evolving record of Kaelen's journey.

The journal permanently accumulates:

* expedition notes
* sketches
* companion marginalia
* field observations
* pressed flowers
* maps
* repaired pages
* burn marks
* blood stains
* integrated reflections

History is never erased.

Later reflections are written beside earlier mistakes.

---

## II. Equipment

**Question**

"What am I carrying?"

Equipment is presented through physical inspection rather than inventory grids.

Weapons tell stories through wear.

Examples:

* chipped edge from Malakor
* repaired crossguard forged by Garrett
* soot from Blackwood Bridge
* leather darkened by sweat
* corruption veins spreading across Nightsteel

Statistics become secondary.

History becomes primary.

---

## III. Camp

**Question**

"How are we doing?"

Camp replaces traditional party menus.

Instead of bars and percentages, companions communicate through behavior.

Garrett may:

* repair equipment
* sharpen traps
* avoid eye contact
* quietly observe Kaelen

Serafina may:

* press herbs
* read old scripture
* stare into the fire
* struggle to hide empathic exhaustion

The player reads relationships through lived behavior.

---

## IV. Memory Constellation

**Question**

"Why am I like this?"

The Memory Palace visualizes Kaelen's psychological landscape.

```
          ★
         /
    ★───★────✦
         \
          ●
```

Visual language:

* Bright stars — defining memories
* Small stars — ordinary experiences
* Broken stars — fragmented trauma
* Dark pulsing stars — unresolved memories
* Golden stars — integrated experiences

Selecting a memory reveals:

* what happened
* how Kaelen interpreted it
* how companions interpreted it
* how it influences current identity

---

## V. Heartstone Sanctuary

**Question**

"Who do I become next?"

The Heartstone is not a leveling menu.

It is a place of reflection.

The player reviews:

* unresolved memories
* companion perspectives
* interpretive lenses
* identity evolution

Progression emerges through understanding rather than accumulation.

---

# Companion Presence Throughout the Interface

Garrett and Serafina should gradually inhabit the interface itself.

Examples include:

Garrett

* tactical annotations
* corrections in margins
* rough pencil sketches
* trap diagrams
* crossed-out reckless plans

Serafina

* pressed flowers
* illuminated script
* healing observations
* translated Eldorian phrases
* notes encouraging self-forgiveness

By the end of the game, Kaelen's journal should no longer feel like it belongs to one person.

It should feel like the shared history of three companions.

---

# World Availability

The interface respects physical context.

| Screen               | Availability           |
| -------------------- | ---------------------- |
| Journal              | Anywhere               |
| Equipment            | Anywhere               |
| Camp                 | Active Campfires       |
| Memory Palace        | Camp or Heartstones    |
| Heartstone Sanctuary | Heartstones only       |
| Journey Archive      | Main Menu or Sanctuary |

World rules always take precedence over convenience.

---

# Psychological Presentation Rules

The interface may communicate uncertainty.

It may never communicate falsehood.

Acceptable:

* handwriting distortion
* delayed page turns
* subtitle persistence
* ink bleeding
* breathing changes
* visual fatigue

Unacceptable:

* incorrect inventories
* false damage values
* fake hitboxes
* fabricated quest objectives
* misleading cooldowns

The player's trust in the simulation must remain absolute.

---

# Closing Constitutional Statement

> **The interface is not a game menu.**
>
> It is the physical expression of Kaelen's memory, relationships, and identity.
>
> Every page turned, every annotation discovered, every scar on a weapon, and every change in handwriting should remind the player that they are not managing statistics—they are witnessing the gradual reconstruction of a human soul.
